  "decision_conditions": [
    "It is considered that ‘on the balance of probabilities’ that the evidence indicates that 128 St John Stree has been used for a continuous period of at least 4 years. On this basis, the use of the upper floors (first, second, and third floor) are immune from planning enforcement action by virtue of s171b of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended). Given that burden of proof, on the balance of probability, has been discharged, it is considered that this application for a certificate of lawfulness should now succeed."
